Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-10-2001||06:09 PM||||I am assembling my 2.8 and I ordered the intake gasket set from the Fiero Store.  BTW, the kit does not include the factory style silicon valve cover gaskets as shown in their pic.  Anyway, the intake gasket given by the Felpro made kit has openings for what looks like a cross-over??  But the old gaskets on my block have those passages closed.  What gives?<P>Also, does anyone know what size o-rings the dip-stick tube and injectors (including cold start injector) take?  I thought this would be included in the intake kit but I was wrong.  Should of phoned first.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Leadfoot||06-10-2001||07:09 PM||||O.K. scratch the second question (found them at Fiero Store).  I still need help with the intake manifold to head gasket.  <P>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Her86GT||06-10-2001||07:12 PM||||I have heard that you can re-use the valve cover gaskets if you have the silicone type and they are not torn.  The injector o rings are also re-useable.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||PJ||06-11-2001||07:19 AM||||If you mean the EGR openings in the gasket it doesn't matter if they're there or not as the passage dead ends in the intake manifold. Don't forget to install the manifold gaskets before the pushrods so you don't have to cut them.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by PJ (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
